\deftab720 {\*\nisusscroll\nisusarea1\xoffset0\yoffset77 }{\pard\nisusnos\ltrpar\pardirnatural\ql\nowidctlpar {\ldblquote The biggest software advance for writers since the word processor.\rdblquote \par
- Best-selling novelist Michael Marshall Smith\par
\par
Typewriter. Corkboard. Scrapbook. Scrivener combines all the writing tools you need to craft your first draft, from nascent notion to final full stop.\par
\par
{\f1\fs26\b Grow Your Manuscript Your Way}\par
\par
Tailor-made for creating long manuscripts, Scrivener lets you break up your writing into sections as small or large as you like. At its heart is a simple ring-binder metaphor\emdash gather material and switch between writing, notes and research with ease. Got a great idea but don\rquote t know where it fits? Compose your text in any order you want\emdash write when inspiration strikes and find its place later.\par
\par
{\f1\fs26\b See the Forest }{\f2\fs26\b\i or}{\f1\fs26\b  the Trees}\par
\par
Whether you plan or plunge, Scrivener works your way: hammer out every last detail before typing a word, or carve out a draft and restructure later. Or do a bit of both. All text sections in Scrivener are integrated with an easy-to-use project outline, so working with an overview of your manuscript is only ever a click away, and turning Chapter Four into Chapter One is as simple as drag and drop.\par
\par
{\f1\fs26\b Research within Reach}\par
\par
Need to refer to research? In Scrivener, your background material is always at hand, and you can open it right alongside what you\rquote re working on. Write a description based on a photograph. Transcribe an interview. Or check for consistency against an earlier chapter.\par
\par
{\f1\fs26\b Getting it Out There\par }
\par
Once you\rquote re ready to share your work with the world, turn your manuscript into an ebook or PDF, export to Word, or simply print it out. You can even share using different formatting, so that you can write in your favourite font and still keep your editor happy.\par
\par
Scrivener\rquote s users include best-selling novelists, screenwriters, students, academics, lawyers, journalists and translators. It won\rquote t tell you how to write\emdash it just provides everything you need to start writing and keep writing.\par
\par
{\f1\fs26\b Features}\par
\par
{\ul Get Started}\par
\bullet  Project templates for novels, scripts, essays and more\par
\bullet  Import many different types of file\par
\bullet  Easily split imported text into separate sections\par
\par
{\ul Get Writing}\par
\bullet  Familiar writing and formatting tools\par
\bullet  Easily switch between working on small sections, chapters and the whole manuscript\par
\bullet  Distraction-free full-screen mode\par
\bullet  Scriptwriting mode for screenplays, stage plays, comic scripts and more\par
\bullet  Live word count\par
\bullet  Mark up text with comments\par
\bullet  Footnote support\par
\bullet  Keep \ldblquote snapshots\rdblquote  of older versions of your writing\par
\bullet  Name generator{\nisusselectcaret \par }
\bullet  Set writing targets\par
\bullet  Automatic backups\par
\par
{\ul Find Your Structure}\par
\bullet  Write in any order and reorganise later\par
\bullet  Assign a synopsis to any section, then work with an overview of your manuscript in the outliner\par
\bullet  Plot your ideas using the corkboard\par
\bullet  Fast project-wide search\par
\bullet  Apply custom icons to your sections\par
\bullet  Use document templates for new sections (e.g. character sheets in novels)\par
\par
{\ul Refer to Research}\par
\bullet  Import research\emdash images, web pages, PDF files and more\par
\bullet  View research files or other sections alongside your writing\par
\bullet  Transcribe audio files\par
\par
{\ul Get it Out There}\par
\bullet  Compile to a single document for sharing or printing\par
\bullet  Export to Word\par
\bullet  Print or create PDF files\par
\bullet  Create Epub and Kindle files\par
\bullet  Export to Final Draft\par
\par
Write Anywhere\par
\bullet  Sync with our iOS version (available separately)\par
\par
